# Build output: 2.8 GB ISOs per build, their checksums, and the screenshots
# taken to prove a build boots. Reproducible from build-iso.sh; the ISO glob
# below already covered the images themselves, but the directory kept filling
# with proof PNGs that are evidence, not source.
/dist/
.refresh.log
.refresh-bridge.log
/scripts/e2e/.screentext
/scripts/e2e/__pycache__/

# Generated by `make publish-os` alongside the ISOs.
SHA256SUMS
BUILD-INFO.txt

# Monitor state/logs, written by the installed copy.
.check-published.log
.check-published.state
manifest.json

# Compiled bytecode, anywhere. These were tracked once, so every py_compile
# during a build dirtied the tree and invited itself into a commit. The scoped
# /scripts/e2e/ entry above predates the Python under linux/ and no longer
# covers where the code actually lives.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
